# Split Office — Windsurf Rules

## Project

Local-first analytical workbench in Rust/egui. Workspace-centric (not a spreadsheet). Split-pane layout where datasets, documents, and workflows are first-class objects.

Stack: egui 0.35 · eframe wgpu · Apache Arrow · DuckDB · Polars · serde.

## Structure

All 15 library crates are in `crates/` (flat). Main binary: `app/`. Benchmarks: `bench/`. Docs: `docs/`. Full breakdown in `AGENTS.md`.

## Rules

- Domain crates (`workflow`, `transform`, `lineage`, `expression`) must NOT import `egui` or `eframe`.
- `grid/src/renderer.rs`: all colours are top-level `const`; never add inline `Color32::from_rgb`.
- No `unwrap()` in non-test code — use `anyhow::Result`.
- Scroll hit-tests per split pane use `ui.available_rect_before_wrap()`, never `ui.clip_rect()`.
- Background threads for DuckDB / Polars work; `mpsc::channel` for results.
- Adding a new crate: place in `crates/`, add to workspace `Cargo.toml` members, update `README.md` Project Structure.

## README Maintenance

Update `README.md` in the same commit when: adding/removing a crate · adding a directory · landing a major feature · completing a roadmap phase. See `AGENTS.md → README Maintenance` for the full table.

## Version bumps

Pre-commit hook auto-bumps minor version. For docs-only commits: `SKIP_BUMP=1 git commit`.
